  "experiment_summary": "docs/experiments/sift_stage01_summary.md",
  "extension": "SIFT optional feature comparison",
  "findings": {
    "decision": "Carry ratio threshold 0.75 provisionally into SIFT Stage 2, where similarity and affine RANSAC will determine whether the retained correspondences are geometrically consistent.",
    "interpretation": [
      "SIFT uses 128-dimensional floating-point descriptors and L2 distance, so its descriptor distances are not directly comparable with ORB Hamming distances.",
      "Accepted-match count and spatial coverage are descriptive inputs to later geometric estimation. They are not registration-accuracy metrics.",
      "The ratio threshold remains provisional because Stage 1 does not test geometric inliers or ground-truth registration error."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Stage 1 evaluates SIFT detection, description, and correspondence filtering only. No RANSAC transform is estimated.",
      "The subset is intentionally small and uses tracked monomodal images with controlled transformations and degradations.",
      "Runtime measurements are machine-dependent. The stored 79.382 ms mean detection time and 3.425 ms mean L2 matching time are from the validated target Windows run."
    ],
    "observations": [
      "moon_blur produced the fewest accepted SIFT matches at the provisional threshold with 11 matches.",
      "camera_identity produced the most accepted SIFT matches at the provisional threshold with 791 matches.",
      "moon_blur had the lowest accepted-correspondence spatial coverage at 0.375.",
      "coins_rotation retained 390 accepted matches with full 4 x 4 correspondence coverage.",
      "Relaxing the ratio threshold from 0.60 to 0.85 increased the mean accepted-match count from 341.4 to 380.7. Stage 1 does not establish that the looser threshold is geometrically better."
    ]
  },
